row drains and exits 0 with the approvals banner; the empty-frontier ladder hands the gap census to the intake mint (rows minted in one bookkeeping commit, driven by the same run, deduped on the next idle pass) and counts rung-2 cards off the shared pending read; pause/dirty-trunk/stall/crash-resume keep their serial-loop contracts at lanes=1.\"\"\"\n+method = \"\"\"Run the dispatch loop suite on real git repositories with the real bar: each spine claim moves one item and its worker receives only that item; the next spine item waits for the exclusive lane's return. A parked resume with an empty or multi-item assignment refuses before mutation or launch, while a single-item lane resumes under the barrier; the remaining handback, refresh, pause and recovery checks retain their existing coverage.\"\"\"\n tier = \"Full\"\n expected = \"Satisfies SR-156 AcceptanceCriteria via the LLR-150 detail contract\"\n automated = \"Yes\"\n@@ -1436,7 +1436,7 @@ phase = 4\n [test.TC-145]\n verifies = [\"SR-156\", \"LLR-151\", \"IF-186\"]\n level = \"Unit\"\n-method = \"\"\"Run the integrator claim suite: a spine claim succeeds on an idle station (the deleted safety-class arm, red-then-green); a hand claim while another holder has the dispatch lock refuses naming the lock and leaves the queue untouched, while dispatch_lock_held=True proceeds; a spine batch claims as ONE bookkeeping commit whose subject joins the ids and whose specs all land in active/<branch>/; the claim commits through the shared bookkeeping helper (IF-186) and refuses by name a dirty path it must write - the spec it moves among them - where it once refused any dirty tree; every other pre-existing single-WI claim contract (abandoned-claim re-cut, relink oracle, minted-id rung, bookkeeping-commit audit) holds unchanged; and the helper isolates the checkout (IF-186): the step and its regeneration execute in a scratch worktree cut from HEAD, planned over HEAD so an uncommitted edit hiding a committed link refuses by name while one adding a link widens nothing, with the kit's committed trunk step run rather than an uncommitted edit to it; an owner edit to an in-scope path made while the regeneration is blocked, or while the caller's before-advance step runs, is concurrent drift refused by name, survives byte for byte and is absent from the commit; an uncommitted generator input outside the scope does not shape the committed artifacts; the scratch worktree is removed on success, refusal and crash, one that will not remove named on stderr; and installation writes the commit's paths and advances trunk by compare-and-swap, a refusal inside it restoring what it wrote while leaving and naming an edit made there.\"\"\"\n+method = \"\"\"Run the integrator claim suite: one item claims in one bookkeeping commit; empty and multi-item claims refuse with no partial claim, and a historical multi-item claim record is neither re-claimed nor split. Drive the dispatch-lock, dirty-path, relink, bookkeeping and checkout-isolation arms as before.\"\"\"\n tier = \"Full\"\n expected = \"Satisfies SR-156 AcceptanceCriteria via the LLR-151 detail contract\"\n automated = \"Yes\"\n@@ -1447,7 +1447,7 @@ phase = 4\n [test.TC-146]\n verifies = [\"SR-148\", \"LLR-152\"]\n level = \"Unit\"\n-method = \"\"\"Run the schedule + integrate suites' adjudication cases: the kind classifies exclusive at rank 1 (the reserved slot, pinned by name); an adjudication-only lane's refresh runs NO bar yet still commits a verified Bar-Green attestation whose summary says no-bar, while a mixed batch bars as usual (fail toward the bar); bar = DevStg-Tests reaches check.py as --gate DevStg-Tests (asserted off the recording stub's own argv), an undeclared bar passes no --gate, and a malformed value refuses the refresh naming it.\"\"\"\n+method = \"\"\"Run the schedule and integration adjudication cases: the kind classifies exclusive at rank 1; an adjudication-only lane's refresh runs no bar and records that outcome, while a lane whos